    "result_text": "All 70 tests across 60 test classes pass with 0 failures, 0 errors. Here's a summary of what I implemented for **version 2 of the owner identity**.\n\n## Changes\n\n**1. Version-2 identity derivation** (`util/Households.java`, `util/Localities.java`)\n- Added a shared `Households.IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` constant.\n- `householdId` now folds the `V2` tag into the hashed input (`V2|<lastName>|<postcode>`), so the value changes but stays deterministic per household.\n- `identityKey` now folds `V2` into its hashed input (`V2|<tel>|<email>|<soundex>`), still a 64-char SHA-256 hex.\n- Added `Localities.regionForIdentity(...)` = `\"V2\"` + plain region, used **only inside** the `memberId`. The plain `region(...)`/`timezone(...)` used for the user-facing `locality`, `timezone`, and owner segment are untouched.\n\n**2. memberId** (`controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`)\n- Now built from the V2 region, so every `memberId` (e.g. `V2NSW27786E13D53`) differs from its v1 form and can't reproduce a v1 value.\n\n**3. Response shape** (`resources/openapi.yml`, `mapper/OwnerMapper.java`)\n- New `OwnerIdentity` schema grouping `memberId`, `identityKey`, `householdId`; these were removed from the top level of `Owner`.\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion` (constant `2`).\n- Mapper populates the nested `identity` object and `apiVersion` via a `toOwnerIdentityDto` default method.\n\n**4. Audit event** (`controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`)\n- `OWNER_CREATED` event moved to schema version 2: added `\"schemaVersion\":2`, carries the v2 `memberId` as the primary identifier, and includes the `ownerSegment` recomputed from the v2 identity.\n\nThe `locality` stays the plain region code (e.g. `NSW`), the owner-segment rule is unchanged (`STANDARD_METRO` for a Sydney owner), duplicate/household detection still works since both new and existing owners are hashed identically, and soft-deleted owners are still ignored.",
