    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:146-206`), which delegates persistence to `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`.\n\n## Before the method body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must be an owner-admin or the request is rejected.\n2. **Bean Validation of the request body** \u2014 the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` is declared on the `OwnersApi` interface (`@Validated`), so it fires before the handler. Constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto`:\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max=10)`\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `addressLine1` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max=255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max=255)`\n   \n   A violation \u2192 400 before any logic below runs. (Note: the `Owner` *entity* also carries `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern` annotations, but they are not what validates this request \u2014 the DTO is.)\n\n## Inside `addOwner`, in execution order\n\n3. **Idempotency read/short-circuit** \u2014 reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key was already used and the owner still exists, returns the original owner with **200 OK** and does nothing else (no new create).\n4. **DTO \u2192 entity mapping** \u2014 MapStruct `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)` (id and pets ignored).\n5. **Address validation + normalization** (`applyAddress`) \u2014 requires a non-blank `addressLine1` or flat `address` (else `InvalidAddressException`/400); trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`; sets `addressLine1/2` and the composed `address`.\n6. **Future registration date rejected** \u2014 a supplied `registrationDate` after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException`/400.\n7. **Default registration date** \u2014 if none supplied, set to `LocalDate.now()`.\n8. **Business-day roll** \u2014 `toBusinessDay` rolls weekends and fixed 2026 public holidays forward to the next business day; stored back on the owner.\n9. **Daily limit check** \u2014 if \u2265 100 owners already share that registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException`/429.\n10. **City capacity check** \u2014 if \u2265 50 owners in the same city (case-insensitive) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException`/409.\n11. **Telephone normalization + validation** \u2014 strips separators, assumes `+61` when no country code, drops leading `0`, enforces 8\u201315 digits and per-country length rules (else `InvalidTelephoneException`/400); stored on the owner.\n12. **Email normalization + validation** \u2014 blank \u2192 null; otherwise must match the email pattern (else `InvalidEmailException`/400), lower-cased, and rejected if the domain is a disposable provider (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail \u2192 `DisposableEmailException`/400); stored.\n13. **Postcode validation** \u2014 blank \u2192 null; otherwise must be 4 digits and fall in the region range implied by the city (NSW/VIC/QLD bands), else `InvalidPostcodeException`/400; stored.\n14. **`sharesHousehold` flag** read from the DTO (used below; never persisted).\n15. **Duplicate-identity check** \u2014 builds an identity key from telephone/email/lastName and rejects an exact match against non-deleted owners \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException`/409.\n16. **Region derivation** from postcode/city.\n17. **memberId assignment** \u2014 generates `<REGION><FY><HASH8><Luhn>` from a SHA-256 of telephone+lastName, de-duplicated by suffix; stored.\n18. **namesakeCount** computed and stored.\n19. **bulkSignupWarning** computed (`true` when >80 owners share the day) and stored.\n20. **capacityWarning** computed (`true` when the city holds 40\u201349 owners) and stored.\n21. **householdSize** \u2014 count of household members + 1; stored.\n22. **membershipLevel** \u2014 natural level, capped at one above the max of existing household members; stored.\n23. **possibleDuplicate flags** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold`, looks up a possible duplicate; sets `possibleDuplicateOf` and the boolean `possibleDuplicate`.\n24. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` \u2192 `EntityManager.persist` (new id is DB-generated via `@GeneratedValue(IDENTITY)`). The service method is `@Transactional`. There are **no JPA lifecycle callbacks, `@PrePersist`, or auditing** on the entity.\n25. **Record idempotency key** \u2014 stores `key \u2192 ownerId` in an in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap` on the controller.\n26. **Response DTO mapping** \u2014 `toOwnerDto` computes many derived read-only fields (salutation, displayName, initials, memberId/householdId/identityKey, fiscalYear, membershipPoints/level, locality, timezone, riskFlag, contactPreference, ageBand, ownerSegment, selfLink).\n27. **Audit logging** \u2014 a human-readable `AUDIT.info` line plus a structured JSON `OWNER_CREATED` event carrying a monotonically increasing sequence number.\n28. **Notification side-effect** \u2014 `NOTIFY.info(\"welcome notification enqueued ...\")`.\n29. **Location header + 201** \u2014 sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and returns **201 CREATED** with the DTO.\n\n## Worth flagging\n\n- All the \"custom validation\" (address, telephone, email, postcode, duplicate, capacity, date) is **imperative code inside the controller**, not `ConstraintValidator`s or an `@InitBinder` \u2014 there are none in the codebase. The exceptions are mapped to HTTP status codes by `ExceptionControllerAdvice`.\n- **No password encoding** and **no Spring `ApplicationEvent` publishing** occur on this path \u2014 the only \"events\" are the audit and notification log lines.\n- A large amount of business logic (member IDs, membership levels, household/capacity rules, warnings, idempotency) lives directly in the controller rather than the service layer, which is unusual for the \"conventional Spring MVC service layer\" the project description implies."
